<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Illinois Country</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pays des Illinois</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a> Country was the French name for the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> valley, in present-day Illinois and Missouri. From the late 17th century French settlers founded villages such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaskaskia">Kaskaskia</a> and Cahokia there, and from 1717 it was governed as part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a>, supplying grain to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> ceded it after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a>.</p></div>
